adjudication.rationale:
In `apps/web/pages/api/webhook/app-credential.ts` the code decrypts and parses the incoming `keys` payload via:

```ts
const keys = JSON.parse(
  symmetricDecrypt(reqBody.keys, process.env.CALCOM_APP_CREDENTIAL_ENCRYPTION_KEY || "")
);
```

Both `symmetricDecrypt(...)` and `JSON.parse(...)` can throw (bad ciphertext, wrong/missing encryption key, non-JSON plaintext). There is no try/catch or validation here, so a malformed request or misconfiguration (notably the `|| ""` fallback when `CALCOM_APP_CREDENTIAL_ENCRYPTION_KEY` is unset) will cause an unhandled exception and a 500 response rather than a controlled 4xx error. This is a concrete correctness/robustness defect introduced in the diff.
